# sample-torch-extension Build Analysis

## Executive summary

sample-torch-extension is a native Torch extension. It requires a C++ compiler
and the libTorch ABI matching the selected Torch channel.

## Source Discovery

- Repository URL: https://github.com/example/sample-torch-extension
- Source files: setup.py and native/extension.cpp

## Build System Analysis

- Build backend: setuptools
- setup.py uses torch.utils.cpp_extension.CppExtension for native/extension.cpp
- Repository layout: build files at repository root

## Compilation Requirements

- Native compilation: required, C++
- Complexity score: 8/10
- System libraries: libtorch_cpu.so and C++ runtime

## Dependencies Analysis

- Build dependencies: torch, setuptools, wheel
- Runtime dependencies: torch>=2.13

## Packaging Strategy

- Build against the selected Torch channel and install through that channel's overlay.
